{
  "slug": "open-source-launch",
  "name": "Open Source Launch",
  "type": "plugin",
  "description": "A portable launch-readiness skill that helps maintainers prepare open-source repositories for a clear, trusted public launch. It audits the README, first-run path, proof/demo, metadata, security surface, release hygiene, launch channels, launch copy, and follow-up plan, then reports evidence-backed code blockers, account/platform blockers, and launch blockers.",
  "longDescription": "Ships **1 skill**, `open-source-launch` (Prepare any open-source repository for a clear, trusted public launch).\n\nInstalls with `claude plugin install open-source-launch@claude-community` from `OMARVII/open-source-launch-skill`.\n\nMake an open-source repo easier to understand, easier to try, and easier to trust before you launch it.",
  "compatibility": [
    "claude",
    "copilot",
    "antigravity",
    "codex"
  ],
